1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,900
During the Classic Period, 250 to 900 A.D., it established relations with Mexican highlands and the Maya lowlands.

2
00:00:07,640 --> 00:00:14,420
The site's architecture was primarily made of mud and was notable for the presence of temples, palaces, ball courts, and houses.

3
00:00:15,220 --> 00:00:24,280
In pre-Hispanic times, Caminal Juyu covered an area of 5 square kilometers and consisted of more than 230 mounds, most of which were demolished due to urban expansion.

4
00:00:24,280 --> 00:00:35,340
Currently, 40 mounds are preserved, 9 are protected within the Parque Archaeologico Caminal Juyu, and rest of the mounds are located around housed, malls, schools, neighborhoods, and other places.

